```scala
        val proc = new ProcessBuilder("opencode", "run", "--format", "json", "--model", model, "reply with exactly: OK")
          .redirectErrorStream(true)
          .start()
```

with:

```scala
        val proc = new ProcessBuilder(binary, "run", "--format", "json", "--model", model, "reply with exactly: OK")
          .redirectErrorStream(true)
          .redirectInput(ProcessBuilder.Redirect.from(new java.io.File("/dev/null")))
          .start()
```

Then replace this timeout branch:

```scala
        if !finished then
          proc.destroyForcibly()
          ProbeResult.NotReady(name, s"model '$model' did not answer within ${timeout.toSeconds} s")
```

with:

```scala
        if !finished then
          OpenCodeCliClient.killTree(proc)
          ProbeResult.NotReady(name, s"model '$model' did not answer within ${timeout.toSeconds} s")
```

Do NOT touch: pipelines/ingestion/**, conf/enrichment.conf

Prove: `grep -c 'redirectInput' pipelines/enrichment/src/main/scala/newspipe/infrastructure/llm-data-enricher/OpenCodeModelReadinessProbe.scala`

Stop when the proof prints 1 and the file still compiles.

3. Add connectInput := false in pipelines/enrichment/build.sbt. This line:

```scala
    run / fork := true,
```

becomes:

```scala
    run / fork := true,
    run / connectInput := false,
```

Do NOT touch: Test / fork, the Compile / run override, libraryDependencies, pipelines/ingestion/**

Prove: `grep -c 'connectInput' pipelines/enrichment/build.sbt`

Stop when the proof prints 1.

4. Add stdin isolation to the launcher Popen call in scripts/newspipe. Replace this exact block:

```python
                proc = subprocess.Popen(
                    ["sbt", "run"],
                    cwd=REPO_ROOT / "pipelines" / name,
                    env=env,
                    stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                    stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                    start_new_session=True,
                )
```

with:

```python
                proc = subprocess.Popen(
                    ["sbt", "run"],
                    cwd=REPO_ROOT / "pipelines" / name,
                    env=env,
                    stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                    stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                    stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                    start_new_session=True,
                )
```

Do NOT touch: the relay, wait, stop and status methods, pipelines/ingestion/**

Prove: `grep -c 'stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL' scripts/newspipe`

Stop when the proof prints 1.

5. Create pipelines/enrichment/src/test/scala/newspipe/StdinIsolationSpec.scala with exactly:

```scala
package newspipe

import newspipe.application.ports.ProbeResult
import newspipe.domain.models.RssItem
import newspipe.infrastructure.llmdataenricher.{OpenCodeCliClient, OpenCodeModelReadinessProbe}
import org.scalatest.funspec.AnyFunSpec
import org.scalatest.matchers.should.Matchers

import java.nio.file.{Files, Path}
import scala.concurrent.duration.*

class StdinIsolationSpec extends AnyFunSpec with Matchers:
  private val item: RssItem = RssItem("g1", "https://feed/x", "T", "https://a/g1", None, "Body")

  private def fakeOpenCode(answer: String): Path =
    val script: Path = Files.createTempFile("fake-opencode", ".sh")
    Files.writeString(
      script,
      s"""#!/bin/sh
         |cat >/dev/null
         |printf '%s\\n' '$answer'
         |""".stripMargin
    )
    script.toFile.setExecutable(true)
    script

  private val enrichmentAnswer: String =
    "{\"type\":\"text\",\"part\":{\"text\":\"{\\\"summary\\\":\\\"S\\\",\\\"countries\\\":[],\\\"geoArea\\\":\\\"Global\\\",\\\"topics\\\":[],\\\"actors\\\":[],\\\"urgency\\\":\\\"low\\\",\\\"language\\\":\\\"en\\\"}\"}}"

  describe("stdin isolation") {
    it("enriches when the child would otherwise block on the inherited pipe") {
      val binary: Path = fakeOpenCode(enrichmentAnswer)
      val result = new OpenCodeCliClient("fake/model", 5.seconds, binary.toString).enrich(item)
      result.isRight shouldBe true
      result.toOption.map(_.summary) shouldBe Some("S")
    }

    it("reports ready when the child would otherwise block on the inherited pipe") {
      val binary: Path = fakeOpenCode("{\"type\":\"text\",\"part\":{\"text\":\"OK\"}}")
      new OpenCodeModelReadinessProbe("fake/model", 5.seconds, binary.toString).check() shouldBe ProbeResult.Ready
    }
  }
```

Do NOT touch: existing test files, pipelines/ingestion/**, conf/enrichment.conf

Prove: `cd pipelines/enrichment && sbt "testOnly newspipe.StdinIsolationSpec"`

Stop when sbt exits 0 and both examples pass.
